// Title: Base64 Encoded PowerShell Command Detected
// Sigma ID: e32d4572-9826-4738-b651-95fa63747e8a
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2020-01-29 | Modified: 2023-01-26
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1027, execution, T1140, T1059.001
// Description: Detects usage of the "FromBase64String" function in the commandline which is used to decode a
//   base64 encoded string
// False positives:
//   - Administrative script libraries
// References:
//   - https://gist.github.com/Neo23x0/6af876ee72b51676c82a2db8d2cd3639
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_frombase64string.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "::FromBase64String("
